---
source: packages/tier1/plot/tests/printing.rs
expression: all
---
== no_x
error[Z0401]: `bars` stands a bar at each value of `x`, but neither the plot nor this layer maps a variable to `x`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:18
  |
2 | d.plot(y: units).bars()
  |                  ^^^^ needs `x`
  |
  = help: map it where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: industry)` for a bar of the count of each industry, or `plot(x: industry, y: wage)` for a bar as high as `wage`

== a_height_of_categories
error[Z0401]: `bars` draws each bar from zero to its `y`, but the `y` axis of this plot holds the categories of `shop`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:27
  |
2 | d.plot(x: units, y: shop).bars()
  |                           ^^^^ needs numbers along `y`
  |
  = help: `points` and `lines` are placed on an axis of categories; `bars` needs a number along `y`

== a_height_of_its_own_categories
error[Z0401]: `bars` draws each bar from zero to its `y`, so `y` must be numbers, but `kind` is a Str, which is placed as categories
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:25
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(y: kind)
  |                         ^^^^ categories
  |
  = help: `points` and `lines` are placed on an axis of categories; `bars` needs a number along `y`

== a_place_of_another_kind
note: 1 row with NA in shop or units dropped (line 2)
error[Z0401]: the plot places `shop` as categories along `x`, but `units`, which `bars` maps to `x`, is an Int, which is placed on a linear scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:44
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop, y: units).points().bars(x: units)
  |                                            ^^^^^ `units` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one axis, so what is mapped to `x` must all be categories (a Str or a Category), all be numbers or all be dates (a Date or a DateTime); `category(v)` makes categories of a number

== a_fill_by_a_number
error[Z0401]: `bars` fills each bar in one colour, so `fill` must show categories, but `units` is an Int without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:28
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(fill: units)
  |                            ^^^^^ a colour for each row, not for each bar
  |
  = help: fill by a variable of categories, as in `bars(fill: union)`, or set one fill for this layer, as in `bars(fill: "steelblue")`

== not_a_colour
error[Z0401]: `fill:` of `bars` is "blu", which is not the name of a colour
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:28
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(fill: "blu")
  |                            ^^^^^ not a colour
  |
  = help: did you mean "blue"?

== not_a_position
error[Z0402]: `overlay` is not one of the allowed words
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:32
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(position: overlay)
  |                                ^^^^^^^ expected one of stack, dodge, fill

== a_position_in_quotes
error[Z0403]: expected one of stack, dodge, fill, found text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:32
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(position: "dodge")
  |                                ^^^^^^^ a word, not a string
  |
  = help: write the word without quotes: `dodge`

== no_width
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `bars` is the width of a bar as a share of the gap between two values of `x`, above 0 and at most 1, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(width: 0)
  |                             ^ not a share
  |
  = help: write 1 for bars that touch, or a share such as 0.5 for bars half as wide as the gap; without `width:` a bar is 0.9 of the gap

== a_width_above_one
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `bars` is the width of a bar as a share of the gap between two values of `x`, above 0 and at most 1, but this is 1.5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(width: 1.5)
  |                             ^^^ not a share
  |
  = help: write 1 for bars that touch, or a share such as 0.5 for bars half as wide as the gap; without `width:` a bar is 0.9 of the gap

== alpha_above_one
error[Z0401]: `alpha:` of `bars` is an opacity between 0 and 1, but this is 3
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:29
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(alpha: 3)
  |                             ^ outside [0, 1]
  |
  = help: write 1 for solid bars, or a share such as 0.5 so that what is under them shows through

== no_color_on_bars
error[Z0404]: `bars` has no argument called `color`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:22
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(color: kind)
  |                      ^^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `p.bars(data: Frame, x: Var | Expr, y: Var | Expr, fill: Var | Str, group: Var, position: stack | dodge | fill = stack, width: Float = 0.9, alpha: Float = 1)`

== a_frame_without_the_place
error[Z0101]: no variable `shop` in `the frame`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:28
  |
2 | d.plot(x: shop).bars(data: frame(units = [1, 2]))
  |                 ---- this layer draws `shop`, which the plot maps to `x`
  |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a variable of the frame
  |
  = help: the variables of `the frame` are: units

== bars_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `bars` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | d.bars()
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `bars` takes a Plot first; `x.bars(...)` is `bars(x, ...)`
